            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Truncate the original arguments to three significant figures:1.0058->1.00,6.83251->6.83,20.156->20.1. Each is exactly the lower main argument at the existing addresses (1.0,0),(6.8,3),(20,1), giving captured roots1.000,2.613,4.483 without a fourth-digit correction. This path is internally coherent but does not follow the visible four-significant-figure rounding convention.",
            "misconception": "Fit the argument to the three-significant-digit main grid by truncating before lookup, instead of rounding to four significant figures and using its fourth digit."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "double-correction",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Keep the correctly preprocessed arguments but add each captured correction twice:1.000+2*.003=1.006,2.613+2*.001=2.615,4.483+2*.007=4.497.",
            "misconception": "Apply the fourth-digit correction once for the original argument and again for the rounded one."
          }
        ]
      },
      "repair_reason": "Preprocessed arguments were previously invariant in all three alternatives. A coherent premature-main-grid path now varies all three arguments and corresponding roots, using only the existing lower-main cells.",
      "supplementary_conditions": ["The existing explicit four-significant-figure preprocessing and lower-main additive lookup remain conditional, not historical invention."]
    },
