    {
      "id": "q23",
      "stem_prefix": "The displayed function has domain $[-6,8]$. Use $\\alpha<\\beta<\\gamma$ to name its actual x-axis crossings from left to right, without treating unlabelled graph positions as exact decimal coordinates. Which complete record correctly reads those positions approximately and separately gives the full sets for $f(x)=0$, $f(x)<0$ and $f(x)>0$?",
      "reuse_literal_table_suffix": false,
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "complete",
          "text": "Readings $\\alpha\\approx-4,\\beta\\approx0.6,\\gamma\\approx3$; zeros $\\{\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\}$; negative $[-6,\\alpha)\\cup(\\beta,\\gamma)$; positive $(\\alpha,\\beta)\\cup(\\gamma,8]$.",
          "figure_ids": []
        },
        {
          "id": "turning-as-root",
          "text": "Readings $\\alpha\\approx-4,\\beta\\approx2,\\gamma\\approx3$; zeros $\\{\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\}$; negative $[-6,\\alpha)\\cup(\\beta,\\gamma)$; positive $(\\alpha,\\beta)\\cup(\\gamma,8]$.",
          "figure_ids": []
        },
        {
          "id": "omit-middle",
          "text": "Readings $\\alpha\\approx-4,\\beta\\approx0.6,\\gamma\\approx3$; zeros $\\{\\alpha,\\gamma\\}$; negative $[-6,\\alpha)\\cup(\\beta,\\gamma)$; positive $(\\alpha,\\beta)\\cup(\\gamma,8]$.",
          "figure_ids": []
        },
        {
          "id": "reverse-signs",
          "text": "Readings $\\alpha\\approx-4,\\beta\\approx0.6,\\gamma\\approx3$; zeros $\\{\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\}$; negative $(\\alpha,\\beta)\\cup(\\gamma,8]$; positive $[-6,\\alpha)\\cup(\\beta,\\gamma)$.",
          "figure_ids": []
        },
        {
          "id": "closed-crossings",
          "text": "Readings $\\alpha\\approx-4,\\beta\\approx0.6,\\gamma\\approx3$; zeros $\\{\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\}$; negative $[-6,\\alpha]\\cup[\\beta,\\gamma]$; positive $[\\alpha,\\beta]\\cup[\\gamma,8]$.",
          "figure_ids": []
        }
      ],
      "intent_updates": {
        "task": "Retain the original full zero, negative and positive sets and finite domain. Actually distinguish the graph's approximate crossing readings and the complete zero set, separately from sign direction and strict endpoint exclusion.",
        "unit_reason": "One complete graph-reading/sign-partition record still covers all three original sign tasks. Alternatives now differ genuinely in the middle crossing reading and in the full zero set, in addition to sign direction and strict endpoints. Named actual crossings give exact sets without inventing exact coordinates; the supplied graph, not an invariant answer list, supports the readings.",
        "limitations": [
          "Complete-record recognition does not establish independently constructing the zero/sign sets or writing their proof. The original supplies the graph; no original drawing task is substituted.",
          "Graph pixels do not establish exact decimal crossing coordinates. The existing actual-figure observations are reused; approximate readings remain approximate and exact sets use the actual named crossings."
