            "misconception": "Use the abscissa of the curve's lowest interior turning point as the middle zero, confusing a local extremum with an x-axis intersection."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "omit-middle",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Read all three crossing locations correctly but collect only the two outer ones into the zero set, omitting beta despite its actual axis intersection. The strict-sign intervals do not include beta; its omission leaves the domain without the required full zero/sign partition.",
